   "evidence": "17 modules import this helper non-publicly, including both direct templates: `Algebra/Lie/UniversalEnveloping/Kostant/RootSubgroup/Scheme/ClosedImmersion.lean:11` and `LinearAlgebra/RootSystem/SimplyConnectedRootDatum/GeckLattice/ClosedRootSubgroup.lean:10` (`import TauCeti.CategoryTheory.Comma.Over`), the latter while publicly importing only its `ClosedSubgroupScheme` chain and defining the identical `rootSubgroupClosedSubgroup`/`rootSubgroupClosedSubgroupIso` API; `Algebra/AlgebraicGroup/Symplectic/DiagonalTorus/ClosedImmersion.lean:11` does the same. The new file is the only closed-immersion module making it public; TauCeti/CategoryTheory/Comma/Over.lean:35 shows its sole content is the `isIso_left` instance.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/AlgebraicGroup/GeneralLinear/Root/ClosedImmersion.lean",
   "fix": "Demote to `import TauCeti.CategoryTheory.Comma.Over` and add the same non-public `import TauCeti.CategoryTheory.Comma.Over` to TauCeti/Algebra/AlgebraicGroup/SpecialLinear/RootSubgroup/ClosedImmersion.lean, which needs the instance in its own proof. Keep the `public import` of `...GroupScheme.ClosedSubgroup` there, since `ClosedSubgroupScheme` does occur in statements.",
   "issue": "`public import TauCeti.CategoryTheory.Comma.Over` re-exports a proof-only dependency: that module supplies only the `CategoryTheory.Over.isIso_left` instance, used in the `MorphismProperty.cancel_left_of_respectsIso`/`cancel_right_of_respectsIso` steps at lines 75-76; no statement in the file mentions anything from it. The same header already marks its other proof-only dependency (`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineGroupScheme.ClosedImmersion`, line 10) non-public, so the instance leaks to every downstream importer by oversight, including the new SpecialLinear module which relies on the leak for its own line 58-59 proof.",
   "line": "11"
  }
